<title>USA: Union Texas says Q2 average oil price fell.</title>
<headline>Union Texas says Q2 average oil price fell.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union Texas Petroleum Holdings Inc said Wednesday said its average sales price for a barrel of oil fell to $16.48 in the second quarter of 1997 from $18.14 a barrel in quarter a year ago.</p>
<p>The company, in a report on its second quarter results, said earnings per share in the period were $0.30, down from $0.35 a year ago.</p>
<p>Net income for the latest quarter was $25 million, versus $31 million in the comparable period a year ago, it said.</p>
